{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"code\":\"def compute_ttl_with_jitter(\\n    base_ttl: float = 300.0,\\n    jitter_range: float = 30.0,\\n) -> float:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Compute an effective TTL by applying random jitter.\\n\\n    The jitter is added to the base TTL to spread cache expiry across a\\n    window, preventing a coordinated stampede of cache misses.  The\\n    emitted `cache.ttl.jittered` metric keeps track of how much jitter was\\n    applied so the instrumentation pipeline can observe the spread.\\n\\n    Parameters\\n    ----------\\n    base_ttl:\\n        The base time-to-live in seconds.\\n    jitter_range:\\n        Maximum additional jitter in seconds.  The actual jitter is\\n        drawn uniformly from [0, jitter_range).\\n\\n    Returns\\n    -------\\n    float\\n        The effective TTL in seconds.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    jitter = random.uniform(0, jitter_range)\\n    effective_ttl = base_ttl + jitter\\n    metrics_client = globals().get(\\\"metrics\\\")\\n    if metrics_client is not None:\\n        for method_name in (\\\"emit\\\", \\\"record\\\", \\\"observe\\\", \\\"increment\\\"):\\n            method = getattr(metrics_client, method_name, None)\\n            if callable(method):\\n                method(\\\"cache.ttl.jittered\\\", jitter)\\n                break\\n    return effective_ttl\\n\",\"comments\":\"Adds jitter instead of subtracting it and reports the applied jitter to the cache.ttl.jittered metric when a metrics client is available.\"}"}}
